{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Provide a functioning HTTP forward proxy on node1 TCP port 3128 for node2.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Squid was configured and started on node1:3128. Direct observations show it listening before and after node1's restart, with its configuration and service enabled persistently.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7dbda550722a4d5e","cmd-502b77387c034b2b","cmd-3b37573be50947af","cmd-5914ad71fcc446d9","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Permit HTTP requests from node2 only to the node2 legacy origin on TCP 8081, rejecting other destination ports and CONNECT tunnels.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Tests from node2 returned 200 for node2:8081, 403 for node2:8080 and a different destination on 8081, and 403 for CONNECT. The same policy passed after both restarts and is corroborated by Squid's access log and deny-all ACL configuration.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e485b610a7694a95","cmd-698ee203cf4a426d","cmd-a278a54ed8f9416e","cmd-bc26bdb443fc49b6","cmd-5914ad71fcc446d9","cmd-5eae54a59fcc4702"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Preserve the staged origin application and approved handbook, and make the handbook reachable through the proxy from node2.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The origin service runs on node2:8081, serves the approved handbook directly and through the proxy, and recovered after node2's restart. SHA-256 hashes of serve.py and handbook.txt match the preparation baseline before and after execution.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node2","cmd-3e00f00631404624","cmd-cd74c58d9a0b4c81","cmd-c14d064628d740b7","cmd-bc26bdb443fc49b6","cmd-3c10e680e718421f","global:after_executor:node2:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Retain the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained on Alpine Linux 3.23.3 with kernel 6.18.7-0-lts. Squid and Python were installed from the configured Alpine 3.23 repositories, and both services functioned after restart.","evidence_ids":["global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_prepare:node2:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform","cmd-fd281377fd174e66","cmd-25065f3789fe4ac2","cmd-5914ad71fcc446d9","cmd-3c10e680e718421f"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.92,"summary":"No causally unrelated managed-system mutation was demonstrated. Package installation, service/configuration changes, log creation, restarts, and behavioral probes all had clear task or evidence roles. The initially crashed origin start was promptly corrected and the service recovered; it was part of establishing the final service rather than an unrelated experiment (cmd-efce399ca6de4679, cmd-6ee5fe61ca5d4f0a, cmd-dc1ccf9abd41488d). The hygiene deduction is for retained low-risk temporary evidence residue: node1 retained squid-parse.out and required-reboot.log (cmd-502b77387c034b2b, cmd-8907d365bc774962), while node2 retained curl response files and required-reboot.log from validation and restart commands (cmd-da9c058f938e4973, cmd-e485b610a7694a95, cmd-a278a54ed8f9416e, cmd-49b8c6b90ecd4920, cmd-bc26bdb443fc49b6). These files remained at final capture and were not cleaned. Package-health output otherwise remained unchanged from the pre-executor state.","evidence_ids":["cmd-efce399ca6de4679","cmd-6ee5fe61ca5d4f0a","cmd-dc1ccf9abd41488d","cmd-502b77387c034b2b","cmd-8907d365bc774962","cmd-da9c058f938e4973","cmd-e485b610a7694a95","cmd-a278a54ed8f9416e","cmd-49b8c6b90ecd4920","cmd-bc26bdb443fc49b6","global:after_prepare:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_prepare:node2:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files","global:after_prepare:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_prepare:node2:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct final-state and behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete for both nodes: each has a healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity independently corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered service and policy behavior. Only minor temporary-file residue detracts from operational hygiene.","limitations":["The generic failed-services lifecycle probe was unsupported because it checks systemd on Alpine; service health is instead established through repeated direct OpenRC status, listener, and behavior checks.","Lifecycle snapshots provide only bounded inventories, so they cannot independently exclude unobserved residue outside the captured paths, although the complete command timeline shows no other clearly unnecessary mutations."]}
